  "result": "**Verdict: `OK`** — one gate run of six used.\n\n**Body** (`library/TrafficSpec/Concepts/interaction/vehicle_file.lean`):\n\n```\ncount over road users v of\n    v = u\n  ∨ (rel_same_direction v u [same_direction_tolerance]\n     ∧ (rel_ahead_behind_in_lane v u ∨ rel_ahead_behind_in_lane u v)\n     ∧ rel_surface_gap u v ≤ file_reach)\n  ≥ min_member_count\n```\n\nAll three claimed atoms used, nothing else; `v` is anchored to the formal `u` by every relation; no magnitude of the file's own.\n\n**Three narrowings declared**: the reach read as the gap's length with an inclusive bound; u counted as a member by identity (the relations are degenerate for u with itself, so a conjunction-only reading could never count it); the one ahead/behind atom read in both directions.\n\n**Witnesses**: one east-bound lane, 5 m × 2 m cars on the centre line at 20 m/s, instance `min_member_count` 3, `file_reach` 50 m, tolerance 0.95.\n- `holds` — five cars 25 m apart (20 m body gaps): u plus two others within reach → count 3, compliant.\n- `fails` — u alone, nearest car 400 m ahead (395 m gap, decided not a member) → count 1, violated.\n- `blind` — the same five cars with the gap *measured* by the source and no extents supplied, so masking `rel.surface_gap` leaves nothing to compute it from: compliant unmasked, unknown masked. Supplying that gap (and the in-lane order) is admissible there because Core cannot compute either without footprints or observed occupancy; `rel.same_direction` is still left to Core's own computation from the headings.\n\nReport in `/local-scratch2/sma407/scratch_core/launch/remote/pipeline/traffic-spec-agent/results/demo22-1109-0108/iter-001/code/concept__drv_interaction_vehicle_file/task_result.md`. No record defect and no dependency defect to file.",
